e said belonged to  a cow that had already been put out of  the herd to be sent somewhere and he  said that was the match and he ran the  calf out and after a while my father had  a conversation with him and said Rastus  that calf doesn't belong to that cow  why'd you run that one out that's  they're not a pair and Rastus said well  they are too well I know that calf and I  know that cow and of course they're a  pair and my father insisted that that  wasn't the case  and  just grew so angry that he went home  that evening and he packed up and he  went to Duncan and he said I'm through  I'm through  if you can't trust what I say around  here I'm finished with this outfit and  he didn't come back and we couldn't  believe it that he was gone and I think  a week went by and he didn't come back  and another week and we just couldn't  stand it because he was part of the  family so finally my father went into  Duncan to try to locate Rastus and he  asked around town and finally found him  and had a conversation with him and  persuaded him to come back and give the  Lazy be another try but my father never  challenged anything Resta said again I  can tell you that there's also an  interesting story about Erastus and your  father and a cult that your father ended  up killing when I mean not a cult but a  calf and and the problem of getting the  mother to know what this nurse nurse  except the camp yeah and how did that  what was that all about were you  involved in that yourself well I saw him  do it a lot of times Rastus was amazing  in his ability to work with the cattle  and we raised our cattle to look alike  to look exactly alike cow buyers wanted  uniform appearance and I tell you I  think Rastus knew every cow and every  calf on the place the thousands of them  he just wasn't wrong about them  and if a mother cow is nursing a calf a  calf is still dependent on the mother's  milk if something happens to the calf  the mother cow won't accept other calves  that aren't her